# The drift of the energy over 2000 steps of the trajectory of
# dist-trajectory-lj.test on domains, with about 124 migrations
# (D399). After 2000 steps the trajectories on domains
# and on one domain have separated, as two runs of a chaotic system whose
# sums are added in other orders do, so they are compared by the change of
# the total energy since the start, against the kinetic energy (about 73),
# with the existing route (one domain) as the reference (docs/validation.md,
# Section 2, rule 4). Measured: in double 1.1e-4 on domains and 1.3e-4 on
# one domain, in mixed 9.0e-5 and 2.9e-4, the fluctuation of velocity Verlet
# at the step 0.005. The bound is 2e-3 for both, about seven times the
# change of the existing route. The fields carried through the branches are
# checked as in dist-trajectory-lj.test, over all 2000 steps; the other
# checks are given the bound 1e30, which every difference meets.
#
# RUN: sed 's/GRID/2, 2, 2/; s/STEPS/2000/; s/XTOL/1.0e30/; s/VTOL/1.0e30/; s/FTOL/1.0e30/; s/ETOL/1.0e30/; s/DTOL/2.0e-3/' %S/Inputs/dist-trajectory-lj.mlir \
# RUN: | mdir-opt --md-exec-assign-algebra --convert-md-dist-to-loops %md_passes \
# RUN:     --convert-md-to-md-exec="skin=0.2 width=64" %md_exec_passes \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_loops_to_llvm \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s
# RUN: sed 's/GRID/2, 2, 2/; s/STEPS/2000/; s/XTOL/1.0e30/; s/VTOL/1.0e30/; s/FTOL/1.0e30/; s/ETOL/1.0e30/; s/DTOL/2.0e-3/' %S/Inputs/dist-trajectory-lj.mlir \
# RUN: | mdir-opt --md-exec-assign-algebra --convert-md-dist-to-md-exec="functions=main" \
# RUN:     --convert-md-dist-to-loops %md_passes \
# RUN:     --convert-md-to-md-exec="skin=0.2 width=64" %md_exec_transforms \
# RUN:     --md-exec-assign-precision="mode=mixed" \
# RUN:     --md-exec-assign-algebra --md-exec-assign-storage --convert-md-exec-to-loops \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_loops_to_llvm \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s
# RUN: sed 's/GRID/16, 1, 1/; s/STEPS/2000/; s/XTOL/1.0e30/; s/VTOL/1.0e30/; s/FTOL/1.0e30/; s/ETOL/1.0e30/; s/DTOL/2.0e-3/' %S/Inputs/dist-trajectory-lj.mlir \
# RUN: | mdir-opt --md-exec-assign-algebra --convert-md-dist-to-loops %md_passes \
# RUN:     --convert-md-to-md-exec="skin=0.2 width=64" %md_exec_passes \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_loops_to_llvm \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s

# The rebuilds, then the checks: positions, velocities, forces, three
# energies, the two drifts, and the two checks of the carried fields, each
# its difference and 1.
# CHECK: {{^[1-9][0-9]+$}}
# CHECK-NEXT: {{^1$}}
# CHECK-COUNT-10: {{^1$}}
